    <item ident="gd822323a013fcd1e03c17b764baaf8de" title="Question 33">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1.0</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>50253,39607,80363,80119</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;According to the reading, what makes a topic sentence too weak to guide a paragraph effectively?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="50253">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">It is too vague and does not give the paragraph a specific, focused direction.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="39607">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">It is too long and contains more than one sentence.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="80363">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">It appears at the end of the paragraph instead of the beginning.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="80119">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">It repeats the same words used in the thesis statement.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">39607</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="39607_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">80363</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="80363_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">80119</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="80119_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">50253</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="39607_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">A weak topic sentence is one that is too vague to guide the paragraph. For example, "Online education has many aspects" does not tell the reader what specific aspect will be discussed. A topic sentence is one sentence by definition, so length is not the issue. Placement within a paragraph and word repetition can affect clarity, but they do not determine what makes a topic sentence weak.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="80363_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">A weak topic sentence is one that is too vague to guide the paragraph. For example, "Online education has many aspects" does not tell the reader what specific aspect will be discussed. A topic sentence is one sentence by definition, so length is not the issue. Placement within a paragraph and word repetition can affect clarity, but they do not determine what makes a topic sentence weak.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="80119_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">A weak topic sentence is one that is too vague to guide the paragraph. For example, "Online education has many aspects" does not tell the reader what specific aspect will be discussed. A topic sentence is one sentence by definition, so length is not the issue. Placement within a paragraph and word repetition can affect clarity, but they do not determine what makes a topic sentence weak.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
    <item ident="gdaf1fec9a669282688231bd46a47b14b" title="Question 34">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1.0</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>563,74161,32132,7633</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;According to the reading, what should a writer do after writing a first draft of a thesis statement?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="563">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Test the thesis by asking whether it can be supported with evidence, is specific enough, and takes a clear position.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="74161">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Ask AI to rewrite the thesis so it sounds more professional and focused.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="32132">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Submit the thesis to the instructor for feedback before writing the rest of the essay.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="7633">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Replace the thesis with a topic sentence that covers the same idea.</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">74161</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="74161_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">32132</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="32132_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">7633</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="7633_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">563</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="74161_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">After drafting a thesis, the reading instructs writers to test it by asking three questions: Can it be supported with evidence? Is it specific enough? Does it take a clear position? Asking AI to rewrite it removes the skill-building from the process. Submitting only the thesis or replacing it with a topic sentence are not steps described in the reading.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="32132_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">After drafting a thesis, the reading instructs writers to test it by asking three questions: Can it be supported with evidence? Is it specific enough? Does it take a clear position? Asking AI to rewrite it removes the skill-building from the process. Submitting only the thesis or replacing it with a topic sentence are not steps described in the reading.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="7633_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">After drafting a thesis, the reading instructs writers to test it by asking three questions: Can it be supported with evidence? Is it specific enough? Does it take a clear position? Asking AI to rewrite it removes the skill-building from the process. Submitting only the thesis or replacing it with a topic sentence are not steps described in the reading.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
    <item ident="g55816463b1fbbda1a3a70b6897cd111d" title="Question 35">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1.0</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>79982,72982,63715,39587</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;What does the term &lt;em&gt;angle&lt;/em&gt; mean in academic writing?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="79982">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">The specific viewpoint or focus a writer takes on a topic</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="72982">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">The length of the thesis statement</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="63715">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">The number of supporting points used in an essay</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="39587">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">The type of evidence used to support an argument</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">72982</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="72982_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">63715</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="63715_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">39587</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="39587_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">79982</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="72982_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">An angle is the specific viewpoint or focus a writer brings to a topic. It is not about length, the number of supporting points, or the type of evidence. For example, a writer could choose many different angles on the topic of online education, such as its benefits for working adults, its challenges for students without internet access, or its effect on student performance. The angle the writer chooses shapes the entire essay.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="63715_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">An angle is the specific viewpoint or focus a writer brings to a topic. It is not about length, the number of supporting points, or the type of evidence. For example, a writer could choose many different angles on the topic of online education, such as its benefits for working adults, its challenges for students without internet access, or its effect on student performance. The angle the writer chooses shapes the entire essay.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="39587_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">An angle is the specific viewpoint or focus a writer brings to a topic. It is not about length, the number of supporting points, or the type of evidence. For example, a writer could choose many different angles on the topic of online education, such as its benefits for working adults, its challenges for students without internet access, or its effect on student performance. The angle the writer chooses shapes the entire essay.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
    <item ident="g5cddbb3a1859ea7219bdbea1d294d357" title="Question 36">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1.0</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>41639,46159,81418,12215</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Which of the following best describes what &lt;em&gt;evidence &lt;/em&gt;means in academic writing?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="41639">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Facts, examples, or observations presented to support a conclusion or statement</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="46159">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">The personal opinion of the writer stated clearly in the thesis</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="81418">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Background information that introduces the reader to the topic</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="12215">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">A general summary of the topic</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">46159</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="46159_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">81418</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="81418_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">12215</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="12215_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">41639</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="46159_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">Evidence consists of facts, examples, or observations that support a claim. A writer's personal opinion is a position, not evidence. Background information introduces a topic but does not support a specific claim. A general summary of the topic is not considered evidence.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="81418_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">Evidence consists of facts, examples, or observations that support a claim. A writer's personal opinion is a position, not evidence. Background information introduces a topic but does not support a specific claim. A general summary of the topic is not considered evidence.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="12215_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">Evidence consists of facts, examples, or observations that support a claim. A writer's personal opinion is a position, not evidence. Background information introduces a topic but does not support a specific claim. A general summary of the topic is not considered evidence.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
    <item ident="g1dcde2a615f2f62003d31ded005b28a7" title="Question 37">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1.0</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>8767,49936,30181,20065</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;According to the reading, which type of writing task requires you to produce a clean, usable result where the method of production is secondary?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="8767">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">A product task</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="49936">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">A process task</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="30181">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">A thesis task</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="20065">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">A revision task</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">49936</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="49936_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">30181</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="30181_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">20065</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="20065_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">8767</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="49936_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;A product task focuses on the finished result, such as drafting a professional email or formatting a document. How you produced it matters less than the final output. A process task is the opposite—the learning happens in the decisions you make while working, not in the document you submit. Writing assignments in this course are process tasks.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="30181_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;A product task focuses on the finished result, such as drafting a professional email or formatting a document. How you produced it matters less than the final output. A process task is the opposite—the learning happens in the decisions you make while working, not in the document you submit. Writing assignments in this course are process tasks.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="20065_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;p&gt;A product task focuses on the finished result, such as drafting a professional email or formatting a document. How you produced it matters less than the final output. A process task is the opposite—the learning happens in the decisions you make while working, not in the document you submit. Writing assignments in this course are process tasks.&lt;/p&gt;</mattext>
          </material>
