          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
    <item ident="gc341bf3b40ebb65aeb37229c4061ebd4" title="Question 42">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>71494,39122,1419,9219</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;According to the reading, why is it important to test a thesis statement before writing the full essay?&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="71494">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">To confirm that it takes a clear position, is specific enough, and can be supported with evidence</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="39122">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">To make sure it is at least two sentences long and covers all supporting points</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="1419">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">To check that it matches the format required by the assignment rubric</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="9219">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">To verify that it uses formal language and avoids contractions</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">39122</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="39122_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">1419</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="1419_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">9219</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="9219_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">71494</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="39122_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Testing a thesis checks whether it takes a clear position, is specific enough, and can be supported with evidence. These three questions help the writer know whether the thesis will hold up through the full essay. Thesis length, rubric format, and language formality are separate concerns that do not determine whether a thesis is ready to guide an essay.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="1419_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Testing a thesis checks whether it takes a clear position, is specific enough, and can be supported with evidence. These three questions help the writer know whether the thesis will hold up through the full essay. Thesis length, rubric format, and language formality are separate concerns that do not determine whether a thesis is ready to guide an essay.</mattext>
          </material>
